{title: 154 - When I Survey the Wondrous Cross}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #154 • }
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: F}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 154}
{meta: category Jesus Christ - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Dm/A]When I [C]survey [F/C]thewondrous [C]cross [F/C]On which the [Gm/D]Prince [C7/Bb]ofglory [Dm/A]died,
[Dm/A]My richest [F/C]gain [Gm/D]Icount [F/C]butloss, And pour contempt [Dm/A]on [Gm/D]all [F/C]my [Gm/Bb]pride.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Dm/A]Forbid [F/C]it, Lord, that I [C7/Bb]should boast,
[Dm/A]save [C]in [F/C]the death of Christ, [C7/Bb]my God;
[Dm/A]all [C]the [Gm/D]vain [F/C]things that charm [Dm/A]me [F/C]most,
[Dm/A]I [C]sacrifice [F/C]them to [Dm/A]his [F/C]blood.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[Dm/A]See, [C]from [F/C]his head, his hands, [C7/Bb]his feet,
[Dm/A]sorrow [F/C]and [C]love [F/C]flow mingled [C7/Bb]down.
[Dm/A]Did [C]e'er [Gm/D]such [F/C]love and sorrow meet,
[Dm/A]or [C]thorns [Gm/D]compose [F/C]so rich [Dm/A]a [F/C]crown.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[Dm/A]Were [C]the [Gm/D]whole [C]realm [F/C]of [Gm/D]nature [C7/Bb]mine,
[Dm/A]that [C]were [Gm/D]an offering far [C7/Bb]too small;
[Dm/A]love [C]so [Gm/D]amazing, [F/C]so [Dm/A]divine,
[Dm/A]demands [Gm/D]my [F/C]soul, my life, [Dm/A]my [F/C]all.
{end_of_verse}
